Drain an autorelease pool around the launch work that 0003 runs before `run`

This change applies to zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
after patches/0001–0006.

What it does:
- 0003 runs `finishLaunching`, the app's finish-launching callback and
  `show_initial_windows` before `app.run()`, inside the pool `run` opens,
  which drains only when `run` returns. Anything autoreleased there stayed
  retained until the app quit. A window the callback opened was never
  freed after it closed: it stayed in the window server and in
  `orderedWindows`, so `window_stack` kept handing back its dead handle.
- That work now runs in its own pool, drained before `app.run()`, as
  `applicationDidFinishLaunching:` is inside AppKit's per-event pool.
- Measured on macOS 27 at a9ed59c with the Finder demo's Quit and Keep
  Windows restore (a window opened in the callback), closing the restored
  window: without this patch its window and child panel stayed in
  CGWindowList in 2 of 2 runs of the shipped git build and 2 of 2
  non-incremental path builds; with it they were freed in 2 of 2. An
  incremental build of the same source freed them without the patch, so
  whether the window lands in the pool depends on codegen. Not re-run
  on a Mac for this re-apply.

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0007-launch-callback-pool.patch
---
diff --git a/src/platform.rs b/src/platform.rs
index 62ee9a8..cd6ac99 100644
--- a/src/platform.rs
+++ b/src/platform.rs
@@ -591,6 +591,10 @@ impl Platform for MacPlatform {
             // when it has already happened; the delegate's
             // `did_finish_launching` still installs its observers when the
             // event lands, and finds no callback left to run.
+            // Its own pool: the outer one drains only when `run` returns, and
+            // anything autoreleased here, a window the callback opens
+            // included, would stay retained until the app quits.
+            let launch_pool = NSAutoreleasePool::new(nil);
             crate::launch_trace::phase("finishLaunching_begin");
             app.finishLaunching();
             crate::launch_trace::phase("finishLaunching_end");
@@ -601,6 +605,7 @@ impl Platform for MacPlatform {
                 crate::launch_trace::phase("app_callback_end");
                 crate::window::show_initial_windows();
             }
+            launch_pool.drain();
             app.run();
             pool.drain();
 
